{
  "archive": "wavefunction_ecp.qvf",
  "description": "wavefunction.gto with an effective core potential: NaH, the ECP on Na replacing 10 core electrons, so basis.n_electrons = 11 + 1 - 10 = 2, which the occupations and provenance.n_electrons restate. The ECP has a local part (local: true, l = 2, the highest l of the centre) and s and p semi-local channels, each U(r) = sum c r^(n - 2) exp(-a r^2) with the radial powers n in powers. The section also carries symmetry_labels, the AO overlap matrix (whose diagonal is 1: every shell is contraction-normalized) and the density matrix of the doubly occupied orbital. The MOs are the Lowdin orbitals S^(-1/2); every number is illustrative, not a converged calculation.",
